=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Type

=SUBTITLE Base class for representing a type

    class RakuAST::Type { }

The C<RakuAST::Type> class serves as the base class for describing
types in RakuAST.

They currently are (in alphabetical order):
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Capture>|/type/Type/Capture>
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Coercion>|/type/Type/Coercion>
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Definedness>|/type/Type/Definedness>
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Parameterized>|/type/Type/Parameterized>
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Setting>|/type/Type/Setting>
=item L<C<RakuAST::Type::Simple>|/type/Type/Simple>

=end pod
